split: central: Ignore central connections that aren't peripherals

split_central_connected() handles every connection in the central role.
When something else on the device connects as central (e.g. a module
that reconnects a BLE mouse), each failed attempt is logged as
"<err> zmk: Failed to connect to <mouse>" and runs the peripheral slot
release / start_scanning() path, and a successful one logs
"No peripheral state found for connection".

Return early for connections that have no peripheral slot.

--- a/app/src/split/bluetooth/central.c
+++ b/app/src/split/bluetooth/central.c
@@ -941,6 +941,14 @@
         return;
     }
 
+    // Only handle our own peripheral links. Other central-role connections (e.g. an
+    // app/module connecting to a BLE mouse) have no slot: logging their failures as
+    // split errors and running the slot/scan handling for them is just noise.
+    if (peripheral_slot_index_for_conn(conn) < 0) {
+        LOG_DBG("SKIPPING NON-PERIPHERAL CONNECTION %s", addr);
+        return;
+    }
+
     if (conn_err) {
         LOG_ERR("Failed to connect to %s (%u)", addr, conn_err);
 
